# The badge slot comes back and the second ring slot goes (server/README.md "Badge slot"). Owner request 2026-10-21:
# "tire o slot extra de ring e coloque o badge" (take out the extra ring slot and put the badge there). Applies after
# 0001-0057, on top of 0023 (quivers and the second ring slot) and 0024 (right-click equips); 0023 stays as it is.
#   * items.xml slotType "badge" (written by server/tools/patch_badges.py on the 40 badges): the badge bit only. The
#     decks keep "deckbadge" (the deck and badge bits).
#   * Player::queryAdd: the badge slot (13) takes a badge (the badge bit without the deck bit), so a deck no longer fits
#     there. The deck (12), ship (14), belt (15) and gloves (16) slots take nothing (retired, no client draws them).
#     The ammunition slot (10) takes nothing: 0023's second ring slot ends. 0023's quiver in the shield hand and the
#     one-might-ring check of slot 9 stay (slot 10 is empty after the login move of archery.lua).
#   * getSlotType (the equip hotkey 0x77, right-click equip): a badge goes to slot 13; a deck, ship, belt or gloves
#     item no longer maps to its retired slot.
#   * Game::internalMoveItem: 0023's swap of the rings in slots 9 and 10 goes (one ring slot).
#   * Game::playerEquipItem and Game::chaosUseEquip: no second ring slot (a ring swaps with the worn one, as in
#     stock); a badge is equipment for the right-click equip (chaosEquipsOnUse). The Eternal Moon Badge is a container:
#     a use opens it, as with any container (drag it to the slot).
#   * Unchanged on purpose: MoveEvents::getEvent still runs the ring events for slot 10 and Player::getArmor and
#     queryDestination still name it, so a ring left there from before is de-equipped like a ring when the login
#     moves it out.
